# Jaguar Type 01 four-door electric luxury GT, 2027-
#
# The production Type 01 on the Jaguar Electric Architecture, revealed in New
# York on 6 October 2026: a low four-door fastback GT with a long bonnet,
# short front overhang, extended rear overhang and 23-inch wheels. It is not
# the earlier Type 00 concept: the production car has the taller glasshouse,
# visible door handles and road-legal lamps.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_Type_01
#
# Dimensions 5.235 x 2.021 x 1.403 m, wheelbase 3.200 m (JLR technical
# specification). The master models a 3.350 m wheelbase measured from the side
# photograph, which reads 4.7 per cent longer than the published figure; the
# deviation is recorded and is under a pixel at sprite scale.
#
# Shape reference: official JLR press images. The side view is a true level
# side elevation. The rear three-quarter in the pack is a macro detail rather
# than a full-car view, so the tail was taken from the side view and the front
# three-quarter plus a supplemental full rear photograph. No rear full-car
# press image was available in the first pack.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the JLR launch palette. Visionary Silver, Iconic Black,
# Compelling Blue and Refined Grey are official gloss colours. Weights 3, 2, 2,
# 1, total 8: a very low-volume new halo car, provisional pending the central
# rebase.
#
# Speed 240 km/h; comfort 165/578, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 165. Class 4.
# Orders open early 2027, first deliveries expected in the second half of 2027;
# still in production, so no retire fields are set.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-type-01.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-type-01.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-type-01/ (gitignored; official JLR press images,
# reference use only).
#
# Accepted deviations: the master models a 3.350 m wheelbase measured from the
# side photograph against the published 3.200 m (4.7 per cent, under a pixel at
# sprite scale). The rear three-quarter in the pack is a macro detail, so the
# tail shape follows the side view, the front three-quarter and a supplemental
# full rear photograph. Front bumper recesses and vane counts are simplified;
# the rear lamp bar is a narrow dark-red insert within the ribbed panel, as the
# photographs show the lamp hardware concealed.


obj=citycar
name=JaguarType01(VisionarySilver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2027
intro_month=7
# retire_year=2047
# retire_month=6
speed=240
class=4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=165
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=578

